# comptime_expand.tkr — the §14 B3 ACCEPT host: Family-B `@comptime(...)` folding. Each scenario names
# itself and asserts its announced value through `run` in `main.tks`, so a relapse names itself. A
# `@comptime` call survives Family-A expansion, is typed to a `TCall` marked by the reserved `call_ns`
# sentinel, and is FOLDED post-monomorph by `expand_comptime` into the literal its body evaluates to —
# with the caller's arguments bound as compile-time constants. Nested `@comptime` calls in an argument
# fold bottom-up before the enclosing call.

Feature: comptime_expand — Family-B comptime folding (§14 B3)

  Scenario: comptime_count — @count() folds its constant body 2 to the literal 2
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario comptime_count: ok"

  Scenario: comptime_sum — @sum(3, 7) binds a=3,b=7 and folds (a + b) to 10
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario comptime_sum: ok"

  Scenario: comptime_nested — @sum(@count(), 8) folds @count() to 2 first, then (2 + 8) to 10
    When built and run
    Then stdout pattern = "scenario comptime_nested: ok"
